  "description": "We rigorously tested how to achieve the creamiest egg bites at home. This version features a silky custard-like egg mixture loaded with bacon and savory Grueyère cheese.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: rice starch → cornstarch\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Cooled egg bites can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days or wrapped individually and frozen for up to 1 month. For frozen bites, thaw in the refrigerator overnight. To reheat, microwave until heated through, about 30 seconds, or warm in a 350℉ (175℃) oven until warmed through, about 5 minutes.",
